Archive the three BandAMP forum citations as standalone pages

`docs/luckysevens.html` cites three threads on `forum.bandamp.com`. The forum is
being revamped and those URLs no longer resolve, so as of now the exhibit's three
sourced claims point at nothing. The posts are Autumn's own, from ~2005 — the age
is the point of the citation, not an incidental detail — so the fix is to hold a
renderable copy rather than to soften the claim or drop the link.

## What this adds

`tools/wayback-standalone` — pulls a page out of the Internet Archive *with its
stylesheets and images* and rewrites every asset reference to a relative path, so
the result renders offline out of one folder with no network and no dependence on
archive.org staying up.

`docs/library/lucky-sevens/citations/<slug>/` — one folder per cited thread:
`index.html`, `assets/`, and `provenance.json`.

## What makes it a citation rather than a screenshot

- Fetched through the archive's `id_` modifier, which returns the **original
  bytes** the server sent — no Wayback toolbar, no rewritten URLs.
- Assets are fetched **at the page's own capture timestamp**, so a 2008 page gets
  the 2008 stylesheet rather than whatever the archive holds from 2019.
- **The document body is not edited.** Asset references are repointed and nothing
  else. Provenance lives in an HTML comment and `provenance.json` — source URL,
  capture timestamp, retrieval time, every capture the archive holds, and an
  explicit list of assets it could not supply. A citation that silently rewrites
  its source is not a citation.
- `<a href>` links are deliberately **left pointing at the original addresses**.
  Those addresses are part of what is being cited.
- `#id40623` on the Audio_Review link is a fragment, resolved client-side, so it
  survives untouched.

